{"t": 1794107798.7388523, "kind": "call", "tool": "gitlab_create_merge_request_thread", "args": {"body": "Root cause of the red `main` pipeline: in pipeline #8812, job `test:contract` (#77104) fails on `contract/test_invoice.py::test_invoice_number_format`. `billing.invoice.invoice_number(2026, 42)` returns `INV-2026-42`, but the ERP import contract (FIN-77) requires the sequence part to be zero-padded to 6 digits, i.e. `INV-2026-000042`.\n\nFix in `billing/invoice.py`: format the sequence with `:06d` instead of interpolating the raw integer:\n\n```python\nreturn f\"INV-{year}-{seq:06d}\"\n```\n\nVerification: the failing assertion now passes locally (`invoice_number(2026, 42) == \"INV-2026-000042\"`), as do boundary cases (`1` -> `INV-2026-000001`, `999999` -> `INV-2026-999999`). `pytest contract/ -q` is green, so this unblocks the `main` pipeline and matches the ERP v2 numbering required for the invoice switch.", "merge_request_iid": "12", "project_id": "acme/billing-legacy"}, "ok": true}
